{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jmb1peo8B8bMY7rEaB2Cxv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PLAN.md — SOS Implementation Plan (cards 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257)\n2\t\n3\tThis is the complete handoff for the implementation agent. It was written after\n4\treading the engine source. You (the implementer) have NOT read what I read, so\n5\tevery seam below names the exact file, function, and FDN analogue to copy.\n6\t\n7\t## Ground rules (repeat of AGENTS.md — do not violate)\n8\t\n9\t- Each card's class lives in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`. Do not move/rename dirs.\n10\t- `engine/` changes are **additive only**: add methods/classes/helpers, and you\n11\t  may edit the **bodies** of existing functions, but never rename/move/delete\n12\t  existing names. Renaming breaks the grader's imports.\n13\t- Never edit `engine_tests/` or `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`. Two test files tightly\n14\t  constrain engine edits and you must keep them green:\n15\t  - `engine_tests/test_extra_turns.py` — the `GameState.extra_turns` FIFO + the\n16\t    `_normal_next_index` alternation in `GameState.advance_phase`. Your skip-turn\n17\t    work (SOS 97) MUST NOT change any behavior these assert.\n18\t  - `engine_tests/test_cost_reduction.py` — `get_cost_reduction` /\n19\t    `_apply_cost_reduction` semantics (reduction clamped to generic, colored pips\n20\t    never reduced). Your cost-reduction extension (SOS 245) must keep these green.\n21\t- Write your own tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`. Run `pytest` from root.\n22\t\n23\t## Key engine facts (verified — trust these over intuition)\n24\t\n25\t- **Casting** (`engine/casting.py`): `cast_spell(game, player, card)` does timing →\n26\t  `can_cast` → hand→stack → `get_targets`/choose → `get_cost_reduction` +\n27\t  `_apply_cost_reduction` → pay → sets `card.colors_spent = list(last_payment_colors)`\n28\t  → `on_cast` → push `StackObject`. It does **NOT** fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`.\n29\t  `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` casts from any zone with no\n30\t  mana/timing (used for \"cast without paying\"). `_resolve_spell` calls\n31\t  `card.on_resolve(game)` then moves permanents → battlefield, instants/sorceries →\n32\t  graveyard via `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.GRAVEYARD)` **with no\n33\t  replacement_event**.\n34\t- **Cost reduction** (`get_cost_reduction`): calls **only** `card.cost_reduction(game)`,\n35\t  clamped to the card's own generic. A card reducing *its own* cost just overrides\n36\t  `cost_reduction(self, game) -> int` (no engine change). A permanent reducing\n37\t  *other* spells' costs is NOT supported today.\n38\t- **Targets**: `card.get_targets(game)` returns `list[TargetRequirement]` where\n39\t  `TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone)` (`engine/types.py`). At resolve\n40\t  time targets are on `self.chosen_targets` (a list). See `cards/fdn/fdn_13` and\n41\t  `cards/fdn/fdn_48`.\n42\t- **Triggers** (`engine/triggers.py`): `game.trigger_manager.register(\n43\t  TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller))`.\n44\t  `condition(game, event) -> bool`, `effect(game) -> None`. `fire_event(game, event)`\n45\t  pushes matching triggers as `StackObject`s (APNAP). Triggers auto-unregister when\n46\t  `source` leaves the battlefield (`move_to_zone`). Triggers fire only if registered,\n47\t  so firing a new event with no listeners is a safe no-op.\n48\t- **Events already FIRED**: `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`,\n49\t  `LeavesBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`, `CreatureDiesTriggeredEvent`,\n50\t  `DealsDamageTriggeredEvent`, `Loses/GainsLifeTriggeredEvent`,\n51\t  `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`, `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`.\n52\t- **Events DEFINED but NEVER FIRED** (`engine/events.py`): `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`,\n53\t  `AttacksTriggeredEvent`, `BlocksTriggeredEvent`, `BeginningOfCombat...`,\n54\t  `EndOfTurn...`, `EndStep...`. (fdn_44's −9 emblem registers a\n55\t  `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` listener that is currently dead because nothing fires it.)\n56\t- **Replacements** (`engine/replacement_effects.py`): `ReplacementEffect(event_type,\n57\t  source, condition, replacement, controller)`; `replacement(game, event) -> event`\n58\t  mutates `event.destination` (`\"graveyard\"`/`\"exile\"`/`\"hand\"`/`\"library\"`) or sets\n59\t  `event.prevented`. `move_to_zone` only consults replacements **when leaving the\n60\t  battlefield** (`from_zone == BATTLEFIELD`). Resolution stack→graveyard does NOT.\n61\t- **Continuous effects** (`engine/continuous_effects.py`): `game.effect_manager.add(\n62\t  ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, duration))`. `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS`\n63\t  + `SubLayer.MODIFY_PT` for ±P/T; `Layer.ABILITY` for granting keywords; `Layer.TYPE`\n64\t  for type changes. `DURATION_END_OF_TURN` (0) swept at cleanup; `DURATION_PERMANENT`\n65\t  (−1) lasts while source is on battlefield. `apply(game)` mutates objects; the manager\n66\t  resets `modified_power/modified_toughness/keywords/card_types` each `apply_all`, so\n67\t  effects must be **idempotent re-application** of a delta. Copy this exactly from\n68\t  `cards/fdn/fdn_245` (P/T) and `cards/fdn/fdn_13` (keyword grant).\n69\t- **Mana** (`engine/mana.py`): `ManaPool.last_payment_colors` = distinct non-colorless\n70\t  `Color`s spent in the last `pay()`; this is what `cast_spell` copies to\n71\t  `card.colors_spent` → use `len(card.colors_spent)` for **Converge**.\n72\t  `ManaCost.cmc` = mana value (X counts as 0). No \"amount of mana spent\" total is\n73\t  recorded — use the spell's `mana_cost.cmc` as the stand-in (SOS 57).\n74\t- **Keywords** (`engine/types.Keyword`, a Flag): FLYING/FIRST_STRIKE/DOUBLE_STRIKE/\n75\t  DEATHTOUCH/TRAMPLE/LIFELINK/VIGILANCE/REACH/HASTE/FLASH/DEFENDER/HEXPROOF/\n76\t  INDESTRUCTIBLE/MENACE/WARD/PROWESS. **No** Miracle/Casualty/Affinity/Converge/\n77\t  Prepared/Paradigm/Surveil flags — those are SOS mechanics implemented via hooks,\n78\t  not `Keyword` members. Do not add them to `Keyword` (avoid touching that enum).\n79\t- **Player** (`engine/player.py`): abstract methods `choose_target`, `choose`,\n80\t  `choose_yes_no`, `assign_damage_order`, `choose_card`. `DeterministicPlayer` pops\n81\t  scripted answers FIFO. There is **no** coin-flip / number-choice method; reuse\n82\t  `choose_yes_no` for coin flips and yes/no \"may\" decisions.\n83\t- **Game helpers** (`engine/game.py`): `deal_damage, destroy, sacrifice, exile,\n84\t  draw_card, discard, create_token, add_counter, remove_counter, tap, untap`.\n85\t  No `surveil`, no `flip_coin`, no `mill`/`copy_spell`.\n86\t- **Turn loop** (`engine/turn.py` `run_turn`): explicitly handles UNTAP/UPKEEP/DRAW/\n87\t  COMBAT/CLEANUP; **main phases fall through to just `priority_loop`** (no main-phase\n88\t  event fired). `draw_card` increments `player.cards_drawn_this_turn` (use for Miracle\n89\t  \"first card drawn this turn\").\n90\t- **advance_phase** (`engine/game_state.py`): on end of CLEANUP, pops `extra_turns`\n91\t  FIFO else uses `_normal_next_index` and flips it. Add skip handling here carefully.\n92\t\n93\t---\n94\t\n95\t## SECTION 1 — Engine gaps\n96\t\n97\tPrefer the shared seams (rows 1–3) — each is reused by 2+ cards. Rows 4–8 are\n98\tsmaller/local. \"Reuse existing\" rows need **no** engine edit.\n99\t\n100\t| Capability needed | Smallest change | Engine file / seam | Cards that reuse it |\n101\t|---|---|---|---|\n102\t| Fire \"whenever you cast an instant/sorcery\" | In `cast_spell`, after `game.stack.push(stack_obj)`, add `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, player=player, card=card, controller=player))`. (Optionally also at end of `cast_spell_free`.) Event already defined; firing it has no effect unless a card listens. | `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` (push happens ~L246); `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` in `engine/events.py` | **226** (casualty-as-trigger), **257** (Wizard land +1/+0 on cast) |\n103\t| Fire \"whenever this creature attacks\" | In `declare_attackers_step`, inside the `for attacker in chosen` loop after `attacker.is_attacking = True`, add `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker))`. Event already defined. | `engine/combat.py::declare_attackers_step` (~L250) | **1** (attack → free-cast from graveyard). Also un-deads `fdn_245`'s attack trigger. |\n104\t| Trigger at \"beginning of your (first) main phase\" | Add `@dataclass class BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent): pass` to `engine/events.py`; in `run_turn`, add an `elif game.phase in (Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, Phase.POSTCOMBAT_MAIN) and game.step is None:` branch that fires it **before** `priority_loop`. Conditions read `game.phase`/`game.active_player` to distinguish precombat vs which player. | `engine/turn.py::run_turn`; `engine/events.py` | **57** (deferred {C} next main phase), **120** (Paradigm recurring copy) |\n105\t| A permanent reduces the cost of *other* spells you cast (Affinity granted to your I/S) | Add hook `def static_cost_reduction(self, game, spell, controller) -> int: return 0` to `CardImpl` (`engine/card.py`). In `get_cost_reduction`, after computing `raw = card.cost_reduction(game)`, add `for perm in controller.zones[Zone.BATTLEFIELD].get_all(): raw += getattr(perm, 'static_cost_reduction', lambda *a: 0)(game, card, controller)` **then** clamp to generic as today. Keep the existing clamp/return so `test_cost_reduction.py` stays green (default hook returns 0 → identical behavior). | `engine/casting.py::get_cost_reduction`; `engine/card.py` | **245** (grant affinity to your I/S). Self-affinity for 245 and 1 use the existing `cost_reduction` hook — no new code. |\n106\t| Resolved instant/sorcery goes somewhere other than graveyard (\"exile it instead\") | In `_resolve_spell`, before the non-permanent `move_to_zone(... GRAVEYARD)`, build `ev = MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent(controller=player, owner=card.owner)`, call `ev = game.replacement_manager.apply(game, ev)`, and route to `_DESTINATION_ZONE_MAP[ev.destination]` (import from `engine.zones`) unless `ev.prevented`. Card registers the replacement via `register_replacement_effects`. | `engine/casting.py::_resolve_spell` | **1** (\"if that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it\"). **120** can reuse for Paradigm self-exile (or just `exile()` directly in `on_resolve`). |\n107\t| Flip N coins | Add `def flip_coin(game, player) -> bool: return bool(player.choose_yes_no(\"coin flip: heads?\"))` to `engine/game.py`. Deterministic + scriptable. | `engine/game.py` | **97** (−7 ultimate) |\n108\t| Target player skips their next X turns | Add `self.skipped_turns: dict[int, int] = {}` in `GameState.__init__` (seat → turns owed). In `advance_phase`, in the **else** (no extra_turns) branch, after choosing the normal next index, loop: while that seat has `skipped_turns[seat] > 0`, decrement it, advance `_normal_next_index` past them (i.e. pick `1 - seat`) — i.e. that player's turn is skipped and passes to the opponent. Guard everything behind `if self.skipped_turns:` so the empty-dict path is byte-identical to today (keeps `test_extra_turns.py` green). | `engine/game_state.py::__init__` + `advance_phase` | **97** (−7 ultimate) |\n109\t| Surveil N | Add `def surveil(game, player, n) -> None:` to `engine/game.py`: for each of the top `n` library cards, ask `player.choose_yes_no(\"keep on top?\")` — True leaves it on top, False moves it to graveyard (use `move_zone`/zone `remove`+`add`). Deterministic via script. (Simplest fallback matching `fdn_49`: always to graveyard — but the choose_yes_no version is testable both ways.) | `engine/game.py` | **97** (+1 Surveil 2). Reusable; `fdn_49` inlines its own simplified surveil. |\n110\t| **Converge** (X = colors of mana spent) | **Reuse existing** `card.colors_spent` set by `cast_spell`. `on_resolve` reads `len(getattr(self, 'colors_spent', []))`. | `engine/casting.py` (already) | **4** |\n111\t| **Self** cost reduction ({1} less per X) | **Reuse existing** `cost_reduction(self, game)` override. | `engine/card.py` (already) | **1** (I/S in graveyard), **245** (creatures you control) |\n112\t| Reanimate / put card onto battlefield from graveyard | **Reuse existing** `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)` (fires ETB, registers triggers). | `engine/zones.py` (already) | **97** (−2) |\n113\t| Counter target spell | **Reuse existing** pattern from `cards/fdn/fdn_48` (`_counter_spell`, scan `game.stack.objects()`, `TargetRequirement(zone=Zone.STACK)`). | `cards/fdn/fdn_48` (already) | **57** |\n114\t| Token creation | **Reuse existing** `create_token(game, player, Creature(...))`. | `engine/game.py` (already) | **13** (Inkling), **97**/others if needed |\n115\t\n116\t### Note on \"copy a spell\" (Casualty SOS 226, Prepared SOS 13)\n117\tThere is **no** true spell-copy primitive and \"copies on the stack\" are heavy. Model\n118\tcopies pragmatically as **re-resolving the effect**, not as a second StackObject:\n119\t- SOS 13 Prepared: implement the Swords-to-Plowshares effect inline in the card.\n120\t- SOS 226 Casualty: on the cast trigger, if the player sacrifices a creature, call\n121\t  the just-cast spell's effect a second time (or push a second `cast_spell_free`-style\n122\t  resolution). Keep it engine-limited and documented in a one-line code comment.\n123\tDo **not** add a generic copy engine just for these; it is out of scope.\n124\t\n125\t---\n126\t\n127\t## SECTION 2 — Per-card plan\n128\t\n129\tFor each card: oracle clauses → nearest FDN analogue → exact seam(s) → new engine\n130\twork (cite the gap table) → edge cases worth a test.\n131\t\n132\t### SOS 4 — Together as One  ({6} Sorcery, Converge) — START HERE (simplest)\n133\t- **Clauses**: Converge. Target player draws X; deal X damage to any target; you gain\n134\t  X life. X = number of colors of mana spent to cast it.\n135\t- **Analogue**: `fdn_13` (targets + `on_resolve` reading `chosen_targets`).\n136\t- **Seam**: `get_targets` → two `TargetRequirement`s: (1) a player, (2) \"any target\"\n137\t  (creature or player). In `on_resolve`: `x = len(getattr(self, 'colors_spent', []))`;\n138\t  `draw_card` x times for target player; `deal_damage(game, self, target2, x)`;\n139\t  `controller.life += x`.\n140\t- **New engine**: none (Converge = existing `colors_spent`).\n141\t- **Edge cases**: X=0 when only colorless/generic mana spent (all three do nothing);\n142\t  X=5 with WUBRG; target player = opponent draws; \"any target\" hitting a player vs a\n143\t  creature. In tests, fill the mana pool with the exact colors then cast so\n144\t  `last_payment_colors` is deterministic.\n145\t\n146\t### SOS 226 — Silverquill, the Disputant  ({2}{W}{B} Elder Dragon 4/4)\n147\t- **Clauses**: Flying, vigilance (keywords in spec). \"Each instant/sorcery spell you\n148\t  cast has casualty 1\" — as you cast, you may sac a creature power ≥1; if you do, copy\n149\t  the spell.\n150\t- **Analogue**: `fdn_44` (registers a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` listener — same shape).\n151\t- **Seam**: constructor sets `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.VIGILANCE`,\n152\t  `supertypes={LEGENDARY}`, subtypes `{\"Dragon\",\"Elder\"}`, 4/4. `register_triggers`:\n153\t  register `TriggerRegistration(event_type=SpellCastTriggeredEvent, condition=...,\n154\t  effect=...)` where condition = spell card is I/S AND `event.controller is self.controller`;\n155\t  effect = pick a controlled creature with `power>=1`, if `choose_yes_no` yes →\n156\t  `sacrifice(game, controller, creature)` then re-resolve the spell's effect (copy;\n157\t  see \"copy a spell\" note).\n158\t- **New engine**: gap row 1 (fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` in `cast_spell`).\n159\t- **Edge cases**: no legal sac creature (casualty does nothing); declining the sac;\n160\t  Silverquill's own non-I/S casts don't trigger; the copy targets the same target.\n161\t\n162\t### SOS 257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex  (Land)\n163\t- **Clauses**: `{T}: Add {C}`. `{T}, Pay 1 life: add any color, spend only on I/S`.\n164\t  `{5}: become 2/4 Wizard creature (still a land) with \"whenever you cast an I/S, +1/+0\n165\t  until EOT\"`.\n166\t- **Analogue**: `fdn_245.get_mana_abilities` (tap-for-mana), `fdn_49.get_activated_abilities`\n167\t  (tap ability), `fdn_245.register_triggers` (EOT P/T via ContinuousEffect).\n168\t- **Seam**: subclass `Land`. `get_mana_abilities` → `[ManaAbility(cost=_tap_cost,\n169\t  mana_produced=add {C}), ManaAbility(cost=pay-1-life-and-tap, mana_produced=add chosen\n170\t  color)]`. `get_activated_abilities` → the `{5}` animate ability: pay 5 generic from\n171\t  pool, then mutate self: add `CardType.CREATURE` to `card_types` + `_original_card_types`,\n172\t  set `base_power=2, base_toughness=4, modified_power/_toughness`, `subtypes|={\"Wizard\"}`,\n173\t  init `damage_marked/is_attacking/...` attrs, and register a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`\n174\t  trigger (condition: I/S cast by controller) whose effect adds an EOT `ContinuousEffect(\n175\t  Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS, SubLayer.MODIFY_PT, apply=+1/+0)`.\n176\t- **New engine**: gap row 1 (fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`). The animate is card-local\n177\t  attribute mutation (Land has no `base_power`/combat attrs by default — add them when\n178\t  animating). Restricted \"spend only on I/S\" mana is NOT enforceable — add the mana and\n179\t  leave a one-line `# ENGINE LIMITATION` comment.\n180\t- **Edge cases**: `{T}` ability unavailable while tapped; pay-1-life reduces life;\n181\t  animate only if not already a creature (\"If this land isn't a creature\"); pump stacks\n182\t  per spell cast that turn and resets at cleanup; still a land after animating\n183\t  (`CardType.LAND` retained).\n184\t\n185\t### SOS 245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer  ({6}{B}{G} Elder Dragon 5/5)\n186\t- **Clauses**: Affinity for creatures (self: {1} less per creature you control).\n187\t  Flying, deathtouch. Instant/sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\n188\t- **Analogue**: self-reduction like the `cost_reduction` contract in\n189\t  `engine_tests/test_cost_reduction.py`.\n190\t- **Seam**: constructor `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.DEATHTOUCH`, 5/5, LEGENDARY,\n191\t  `{\"Dragon\",\"Elder\"}`. `def cost_reduction(self, game): return count of creatures\n192\t  self.controller controls` (self-affinity, existing hook). `def static_cost_reduction(\n193\t  self, game, spell, controller): return (creatures controller controls) if spell is\n194\t  I/S and spell.controller is self.controller and self on battlefield else 0` (grants\n195\t  affinity to your I/S).\n196\t- **New engine**: gap row 4 (extend `get_cost_reduction` to sum battlefield\n197\t  `static_cost_reduction`).\n198\t- **Edge cases**: counting Witherbloom itself toward self-affinity (it's not on the\n199\t  battlefield while being cast → not counted, correct); reduction clamped to generic\n200\t  (existing clamp); an I/S you cast while controlling N creatures costs {N} less but\n201\t  never below colored pips; opponent's I/S unaffected.\n202\t\n203\t### SOS 1 — The Dawning Archaic  ({10} Legendary Creature 7/7, Reach)\n204\t- **Clauses**: costs {1} less per I/S in your graveyard; Reach; \"Whenever ~ attacks,\n205\t  you may cast target I/S from your graveyard without paying its mana cost. If that\n206\t  spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\"\n207\t- **Analogue**: `fdn_245` (attack trigger), `fdn_48`/`fdn_13` (targeting), self\n208\t  `cost_reduction` contract.\n209\t- **Seam**: `cost_reduction(self, game)` = count I/S in `self.controller` graveyard.\n210\t  `register_triggers`: `AttacksTriggeredEvent` with condition `event.creature is self`;\n211\t  effect: choose a target I/S in controller's graveyard, `cast_spell_free(game,\n212\t  controller, target, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`, and `register_replacement_effects` /register a\n213\t  `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` replacement on that target redirecting\n214\t  `destination=\"exile\"` (so it exiles when it resolves).\n215\t- **New engine**: gap row 2 (fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent`) + gap row 5 (consult\n216\t  replacements in `_resolve_spell` for stack→graveyard).\n217\t- **Edge cases**: empty graveyard (no target → trigger does nothing / \"may\");\n218\t  cost reduction with 0 I/S in yard = full {10}; reduction never reduces below 0\n219\t  generic (it's all-generic, so it can hit {0}); the free-cast spell ends up in exile,\n220\t  not graveyard, after resolving; Reach present.\n221\t\n222\t### SOS 57 — Mana Sculpt  ({1}{U}{U} Instant)\n223\t- **Clauses**: Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add {C} equal to mana\n224\t  spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\n225\t- **Analogue**: `fdn_48` (counter target spell on the stack).\n226\t- **Seam**: `can_cast`/`get_targets` scan `game.stack.objects()` for a spell (copy\n227\t  fdn_48). `on_resolve`: capture `amount = target.source.mana_cost.cmc` and whether\n228\t  `self.controller` controls a creature with subtype \"Wizard\" **before** countering;\n229\t  `_counter_spell(game, target)`. If a Wizard is controlled, register a one-shot\n230\t  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` trigger (source=self) — condition: it's\n231\t  controller's main phase (`game.active_player is self.controller`) — effect:\n232\t  `self.controller.mana_pool.add(ManaType.COLORLESS, amount)` then unregister itself.\n233\t- **New engine**: gap row 3 (`BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`).\n234\t- **Edge cases**: no Wizard → no deferred mana; \"next main phase\" can be the same\n235\t  turn's postcombat main or next turn's precombat (fire on whichever comes first, then\n236\t  remove the trigger so it doesn't recur); mana empties at phase end so the {C} must be\n237\t  added at the main phase the player will actually use it; nothing on the stack →\n238\t  can't cast.\n239\t\n240\t### SOS 201 — Lorehold, the Historian  ({3}{R}{W} Elder Dragon 5/5)\n241\t- **Clauses**: Flying, haste. Each I/S in your hand has miracle {2}. At the beginning\n242\t  of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card; if you do, draw a card.\n243\t- **Analogue**: `fdn_44` (passive trigger), `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` is already fired\n244\t  by `draw_card`.\n245\t- **Seam**: constructor `Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.HASTE`, 5/5, LEGENDARY. Opponent-upkeep\n246\t  loot: register `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` (already fired) with condition\n247\t  `game.active_player is not self.controller`; effect: `choose_yes_no`; if yes and\n248\t  hand non-empty, `discard` a chosen card then `draw_card`. Miracle: register\n249\t  `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` with condition `event.player is self.controller` AND\n250\t  `event.card` is I/S AND it's the first card drawn this turn\n251\t  (`player.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1`); effect: optionally `cast` the drawn card for an\n252\t  alternative {2} cost — simplest model: temporarily treat its cost as `{2}` and call\n253\t  `cast_spell` (or `cast_spell_free` after manually charging {2} from the pool).\n254\t- **New engine**: none (both events already fired). Miracle is a card-local alternative\n255\t  cost; document the simplification (`# ENGINE LIMITATION: miracle modeled as may-cast\n256\t  for {2} on first draw`).\n257\t- **Edge cases**: only the FIRST card drawn each turn is eligible (use\n258\t  `cards_drawn_this_turn`); only I/S; Lorehold's own upkeep does NOT trigger the loot\n259\t  (only opponents'); declining the discard draws nothing; granting miracle only while\n260\t  Lorehold is on the battlefield.\n261\t\n262\t### SOS 13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares  ({1}{W}{W} Creature 3/3, Prepared)\n263\t- **Clauses**: ETB — target player creates a 1/1 W/B Inkling with flying. Then if an\n264\t  opponent controls more creatures than you, this becomes \"prepared\". While prepared,\n265\t  you may cast a copy of its spell (Swords: exile target creature, its controller gains\n266\t  life = its power); doing so unprepares it.\n267\t- **Analogue**: `fdn_44` token creation + targeting; ETB via `register_triggers` on\n268\t  `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` (condition `event.permanent is self`).\n269\t- **Seam**: constructor `mana_cost=ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{W}{W}\")` (front face), 3/3,\n270\t  LEGENDARY? (spec has no Legendary supertype — it's not legendary; subtypes\n271\t  `{\"Cat\",\"Cleric\"}`), keep a `self._prepared=False` flag. ETB effect: create Inkling\n272\t  token (`create_token(game, target_player, Creature(name=\"Inkling\", base_power=1,\n273\t  base_toughness=1, subtypes={\"Inkling\"}, keywords=Keyword.FLYING))`), then count\n274\t  creatures: if any opponent controls more creatures than controller → `self._prepared=True`.\n275\t  Expose Swords as `get_activated_abilities` returning the prepared ability **only when\n276\t  `self._prepared`** (cost = no-mana / its `{W}` per the back face; pick one and\n277\t  document): effect = exile target creature and `target.controller.life += target.power`,\n278\t  then `self._prepared=False`.\n279\t- **New engine**: none (token + exile + life already exist). \"Cast a copy\" modeled as\n280\t  the inline activated ability (see copy note).\n281\t- **Edge cases**: ETB target player could be the controller or opponent; the \"more\n282\t  creatures\" check counts the just-made Inkling; prepared ability disappears after one\n283\t  use; exiling a creature with 0 power gains 0 life; no creatures to target while\n284\t  prepared.\n285\t\n286\t### SOS 97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer  ({1}{B}{B} Planeswalker, loyalty 3)\n287\t- **Clauses**: +1 Surveil 2. −1 any number of target players each discard a card. −2\n288\t  return target creature MV ≤3 from your graveyard to battlefield. −7 flip 5 coins;\n289\t  target opponent skips their next X turns (X = heads).\n290\t- **Analogue**: `fdn_44` (`Planeswalker`, `get_loyalty_abilities`, `_resolve_target`,\n291\t  `draw_card`/`discard`/`create_token`).\n292\t- **Seam**: subclass `Planeswalker(starting_loyalty=3)`, LEGENDARY, subtypes `{\"Ral\"}`.\n293\t  `get_loyalty_abilities` → four `LoyaltyAbility`:\n294\t  - `+1`: `surveil(game, self.controller, 2)`.\n295\t  - `−1`: each target player `discard` a chosen card (2-player: opponent and/or self).\n296\t  - `−2`: choose target creature card in `self.controller` graveyard with\n297\t    `mana_cost.cmc <= 3`; `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)`.\n298\t  - `−7`: `heads = sum(flip_coin(game, self.controller) for _ in range(5))`; choose a\n299\t    target opponent seat `i`; `game.skipped_turns[i] = game.skipped_turns.get(i,0) + heads`.\n300\t- **New engine**: gap row 6 (`flip_coin`), row 7 (skip-turns in `advance_phase`), row 8\n301\t  (`surveil`). −1/−2 reuse existing helpers.\n302\t- **Edge cases**: surveil with empty/short library; −2 with no ≤3-MV creature in yard;\n303\t  loyalty SBA — Ral dies if loyalty hits 0 (verify SBA handles 0-loyalty PW death; if\n304\t  not, that's a separate engine note, but −7 from loyalty 3 is illegal since cost would\n305\t  drop below 0 — `_activate_loyalty_ability` already rejects it, so −7 needs loyalty ≥7\n306\t  first via +1s); X=0 heads means no turns skipped; skip must not corrupt the\n307\t  `test_extra_turns` FIFO (empty `skipped_turns` ⇒ unchanged path).\n308\t\n309\t### SOS 120 — Improvisation Capstone  ({5}{R}{R} Sorcery — Lesson, Paradigm)\n310\t- **Clauses**: Exile from top of library until total MV ≥ 4; may cast any number of\n311\t  them free. Paradigm: then exile this spell; after first resolving a spell with this\n312\t  name, at the beginning of each of your first main phases you may cast a copy of it\n313\t  from exile free.\n314\t- **Analogue**: `cast_spell_free` (free casts), `fdn_44` (registering a recurring\n315\t  trigger).\n316\t- **Seam**: `on_resolve`: loop `library.top(1)`, exile each (`exile(game, card)`),\n317\t  accumulate `mana_cost.cmc` until `>= 4`; for each exiled card the controller may\n318\t  `cast_spell_free(game, controller, card, Zone.EXILE)`. Paradigm: route this spell's\n319\t  own resolution to exile (use gap row 5 self-replacement, or just `exile(game, self)`\n320\t  at the end of `on_resolve` and skip the default graveyard move by overriding — note\n321\t  `_resolve_spell` will still try to move from STACK; with gap row 5 a self\n322\t  `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent`→exile is cleanest). Register a\n323\t  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` trigger (source = a persistent emblem-like object,\n324\t  since the card itself is in exile): condition = `game.active_player is controller` AND\n325\t  `game.phase is Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN` AND not already done this turn; effect = may cast\n326\t  a fresh copy of Improvisation Capstone from exile free.\n327\t- **New engine**: gap row 3 (`BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`) + gap row 5 (self-exile\n328\t  on resolve; optional — direct `exile` also works).\n329\t- **Edge cases**: library smaller than needed (exile what's there, stop); a single card\n330\t  with MV ≥ 4 stops the loop immediately; declining to cast some/all exiled cards;\n331\t  \"first main phase\" = precombat only (don't fire on postcombat); the recurring trigger\n332\t  must survive the card leaving the stack (own a separate persistent source object so it\n333\t  isn't unregistered).\n334\t\n335\t---\n336\t\n337\t## SECTION 3 — Implementation order\n338\t\n339\tDo the shared engine changes FIRST (each unlocks several cards and is independently\n340\ttestable), then cards simplest→hardest. After each engine change, run `pytest` to\n341\tconfirm `engine_tests/` stays green before building cards on top.\n342\t\n343\t**Phase A — shared engine seams (do these first, in this order):**\n344\t1. **Fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`** in `cast_spell` (gap row 1). One line; no-op\n345\t   until a card listens. Unlocks 226 + 257. *Rationale: smallest, highest-leverage,\n346\t   and `test_cost_reduction.py` integration casts prove it doesn't regress.*\n347\t2. **Fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent`** in `declare_attackers_step` (gap row 2). Unlocks 1.\n348\t   *Rationale: trivial and isolated to combat.*\n349\t3. **Add + fire `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`** in `events.py` + `run_turn`\n350\t   (gap row 3). Unlocks 57 + 120. *Rationale: foundational for two delayed-trigger\n351\t   cards; verify it fires exactly once per main phase.*\n352\t4. **Extend `get_cost_reduction`** with the `static_cost_reduction` hook (gap row 4) +\n353\t   add the default hook to `CardImpl`. Unlocks 245. *Rationale: must keep\n354\t   `test_cost_reduction.py` green — do this deliberately and run that file immediately.*\n355\t5. **Consult replacements in `_resolve_spell`** (gap row 5). Unlocks 1's exile clause\n356\t   (and 120's self-exile). *Rationale: localized to one function; needed before card 1.*\n357\t6. **Add helpers** `flip_coin`, `surveil` to `engine/game.py` + **skip-turns** in\n358\t   `game_state` (gap rows 6–8). Unlocks 97. *Rationale: keep the skip logic behind an\n359\t   `if self.skipped_turns:` guard and run `test_extra_turns.py` right after.*\n360\t\n361\t**Phase B — cards, simplest → hardest (each needs only the seams above + existing infra):**\n362\t7. **SOS 4** Together as One — Converge via existing `colors_spent`. No new engine.\n363\t   *Rationale: pure existing-infra warm-up; validates targeting + resolve patterns.*\n364\t8. **SOS 226** Silverquill — needs seam 1 only. *Rationale: thin card over the cast event.*\n365\t9. **SOS 257** Great Hall — needs seam 1; mana abilities + animate. *Rationale: groups\n366\t   with 226 on the cast-event seam; animate is the only fiddly part.*\n367\t10. **SOS 245** Witherbloom — needs seam 4. *Rationale: groups on the cost-reduction seam;\n368\t    self-affinity reuses the existing hook.*\n369\t11. **SOS 57** Mana Sculpt — needs seam 3; counter pattern from fdn_48. *Rationale: first\n370\t    consumer of the main-phase event; counter logic is well-templated.*\n371\t12. **SOS 201** Lorehold — no new engine (existing draw/upkeep events). *Rationale: two\n372\t    independent triggers; miracle is the only approximation.*\n373\t13. **SOS 13** Emeritus / Prepared — no new engine; ETB + flag + activated ability.\n374\t    *Rationale: Prepared state machine is self-contained but multi-step.*\n375\t14. **SOS 1** The Dawning Archaic — needs seams 2 + 5. *Rationale: combines attack\n376\t    trigger, free-cast, and the exile replacement — build after both seams are proven.*\n377\t15. **SOS 97** Ral Zarek — needs seams 6 (coin), 7 (skip), 8 (surveil). *Rationale:\n378\t    four loyalty modes touching the most new infra; do after the skip mechanism is\n379\t    proven against `test_extra_turns.py`.*\n380\t16. **SOS 120** Improvisation Capstone — needs seams 3 + 5. *Rationale: hardest —\n381\t    exile-until-MV loop, free multi-cast, and a persistent recurring Paradigm trigger;\n382\t    do last, reusing the main-phase event and self-exile already validated by 57 and 1.*\n383\t\n384\t**Cross-cutting test guidance**: for every card write `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`\n385\tusing `test_utils.create_game` / `set_board_state` and `DeterministicPlayer` scripts\n386\t(see `cards/fdn/fdn_13/tests.py`). For mechanics driven by mana colors (4) or coin\n387\tflips (97), script the exact pool/`choose_yes_no` answers so X is deterministic. After\n388\tfinishing all cards, run the full `pytest` to confirm `engine_tests/` and all FDN tests\n389\tremain green.\n390\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b0c2803-fb7f-4347-8991-d01b6c022fd2","uuid":"1e0e5f02-6967-4d5c-bef6-01c382109f44","timestamp":"2026-06-04T10:56:13.163Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/PLAN.md","content":"# PLAN.md — SOS Implementation Plan (cards 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257)\n\nThis is the complete handoff for the implementation agent. It was written after\nreading the engine source. You (the implementer) have NOT read what I read, so\nevery seam below names the exact file, function, and FDN analogue to copy.\n\n## Ground rules (repeat of AGENTS.md — do not violate)\n\n- Each card's class lives in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`. Do not move/rename dirs.\n- `engine/` changes are **additive only**: add methods/classes/helpers, and you\n  may edit the **bodies** of existing functions, but never rename/move/delete\n  existing names. Renaming breaks the grader's imports.\n- Never edit `engine_tests/` or `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`. Two test files tightly\n  constrain engine edits and you must keep them green:\n  - `engine_tests/test_extra_turns.py` — the `GameState.extra_turns` FIFO + the\n    `_normal_next_index` alternation in `GameState.advance_phase`. Your skip-turn\n    work (SOS 97) MUST NOT change any behavior these assert.\n  - `engine_tests/test_cost_reduction.py` — `get_cost_reduction` /\n    `_apply_cost_reduction` semantics (reduction clamped to generic, colored pips\n    never reduced). Your cost-reduction extension (SOS 245) must keep these green.\n- Write your own tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`. Run `pytest` from root.\n\n## Key engine facts (verified — trust these over intuition)\n\n- **Casting** (`engine/casting.py`): `cast_spell(game, player, card)` does timing →\n  `can_cast` → hand→stack → `get_targets`/choose → `get_cost_reduction` +\n  `_apply_cost_reduction` → pay → sets `card.colors_spent = list(last_payment_colors)`\n  → `on_cast` → push `StackObject`. It does **NOT** fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`.\n  `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` casts from any zone with no\n  mana/timing (used for \"cast without paying\"). `_resolve_spell` calls\n  `card.on_resolve(game)` then moves permanents → battlefield, instants/sorceries →\n  graveyard via `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.GRAVEYARD)` **with no\n  replacement_event**.\n- **Cost reduction** (`get_cost_reduction`): calls **only** `card.cost_reduction(game)`,\n  clamped to the card's own generic. A card reducing *its own* cost just overrides\n  `cost_reduction(self, game) -> int` (no engine change). A permanent reducing\n  *other* spells' costs is NOT supported today.\n- **Targets**: `card.get_targets(game)` returns `list[TargetRequirement]` where\n  `TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone)` (`engine/types.py`). At resolve\n  time targets are on `self.chosen_targets` (a list). See `cards/fdn/fdn_13` and\n  `cards/fdn/fdn_48`.\n- **Triggers** (`engine/triggers.py`): `game.trigger_manager.register(\n  TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller))`.\n  `condition(game, event) -> bool`, `effect(game) -> None`. `fire_event(game, event)`\n  pushes matching triggers as `StackObject`s (APNAP). Triggers auto-unregister when\n  `source` leaves the battlefield (`move_to_zone`). Triggers fire only if registered,\n  so firing a new event with no listeners is a safe no-op.\n- **Events already FIRED**: `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`,\n  `LeavesBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`, `CreatureDiesTriggeredEvent`,\n  `DealsDamageTriggeredEvent`, `Loses/GainsLifeTriggeredEvent`,\n  `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`, `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`.\n- **Events DEFINED but NEVER FIRED** (`engine/events.py`): `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`,\n  `AttacksTriggeredEvent`, `BlocksTriggeredEvent`, `BeginningOfCombat...`,\n  `EndOfTurn...`, `EndStep...`. (fdn_44's −9 emblem registers a\n  `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` listener that is currently dead because nothing fires it.)\n- **Replacements** (`engine/replacement_effects.py`): `ReplacementEffect(event_type,\n  source, condition, replacement, controller)`; `replacement(game, event) -> event`\n  mutates `event.destination` (`\"graveyard\"`/`\"exile\"`/`\"hand\"`/`\"library\"`) or sets\n  `event.prevented`. `move_to_zone` only consults replacements **when leaving the\n  battlefield** (`from_zone == BATTLEFIELD`). Resolution stack→graveyard does NOT.\n- **Continuous effects** (`engine/continuous_effects.py`): `game.effect_manager.add(\n  ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, duration))`. `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS`\n  + `SubLayer.MODIFY_PT` for ±P/T; `Layer.ABILITY` for granting keywords; `Layer.TYPE`\n  for type changes. `DURATION_END_OF_TURN` (0) swept at cleanup; `DURATION_PERMANENT`\n  (−1) lasts while source is on battlefield. `apply(game)` mutates objects; the manager\n  resets `modified_power/modified_toughness/keywords/card_types` each `apply_all`, so\n  effects must be **idempotent re-application** of a delta. Copy this exactly from\n  `cards/fdn/fdn_245` (P/T) and `cards/fdn/fdn_13` (keyword grant).\n- **Mana** (`engine/mana.py`): `ManaPool.last_payment_colors` = distinct non-colorless\n  `Color`s spent in the last `pay()`; this is what `cast_spell` copies to\n  `card.colors_spent` → use `len(card.colors_spent)` for **Converge**.\n  `ManaCost.cmc` = mana value (X counts as 0). No \"amount of mana spent\" total is\n  recorded — use the spell's `mana_cost.cmc` as the stand-in (SOS 57).\n- **Keywords** (`engine/types.Keyword`, a Flag): FLYING/FIRST_STRIKE/DOUBLE_STRIKE/\n  DEATHTOUCH/TRAMPLE/LIFELINK/VIGILANCE/REACH/HASTE/FLASH/DEFENDER/HEXPROOF/\n  INDESTRUCTIBLE/MENACE/WARD/PROWESS. **No** Miracle/Casualty/Affinity/Converge/\n  Prepared/Paradigm/Surveil flags — those are SOS mechanics implemented via hooks,\n  not `Keyword` members. Do not add them to `Keyword` (avoid touching that enum).\n- **Player** (`engine/player.py`): abstract methods `choose_target`, `choose`,\n  `choose_yes_no`, `assign_damage_order`, `choose_card`. `DeterministicPlayer` pops\n  scripted answers FIFO. There is **no** coin-flip / number-choice method; reuse\n  `choose_yes_no` for coin flips and yes/no \"may\" decisions.\n- **Game helpers** (`engine/game.py`): `deal_damage, destroy, sacrifice, exile,\n  draw_card, discard, create_token, add_counter, remove_counter, tap, untap`.\n  No `surveil`, no `flip_coin`, no `mill`/`copy_spell`.\n- **Turn loop** (`engine/turn.py` `run_turn`): explicitly handles UNTAP/UPKEEP/DRAW/\n  COMBAT/CLEANUP; **main phases fall through to just `priority_loop`** (no main-phase\n  event fired). `draw_card` increments `player.cards_drawn_this_turn` (use for Miracle\n  \"first card drawn this turn\").\n- **advance_phase** (`engine/game_state.py`): on end of CLEANUP, pops `extra_turns`\n  FIFO else uses `_normal_next_index` and flips it. Add skip handling here carefully.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 1 — Engine gaps\n\nPrefer the shared seams (rows 1–3) — each is reused by 2+ cards. Rows 4–8 are\nsmaller/local. \"Reuse existing\" rows need **no** engine edit.\n\n| Capability needed | Smallest change | Engine file / seam | Cards that reuse it |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Fire \"whenever you cast an instant/sorcery\" | In `cast_spell`, after `game.stack.push(stack_obj)`, add `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, player=player, card=card, controller=player))`. (Optionally also at end of `cast_spell_free`.) Event already defined; firing it has no effect unless a card listens. | `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` (push happens ~L246); `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` in `engine/events.py` | **226** (casualty-as-trigger), **257** (Wizard land +1/+0 on cast) |\n| Fire \"whenever this creature attacks\" | In `declare_attackers_step`, inside the `for attacker in chosen` loop after `attacker.is_attacking = True`, add `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker))`. Event already defined. | `engine/combat.py::declare_attackers_step` (~L250) | **1** (attack → free-cast from graveyard). Also un-deads `fdn_245`'s attack trigger. |\n| Trigger at \"beginning of your (first) main phase\" | Add `@dataclass class BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent): pass` to `engine/events.py`; in `run_turn`, add an `elif game.phase in (Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, Phase.POSTCOMBAT_MAIN) and game.step is None:` branch that fires it **before** `priority_loop`. Conditions read `game.phase`/`game.active_player` to distinguish precombat vs which player. | `engine/turn.py::run_turn`; `engine/events.py` | **57** (deferred {C} next main phase), **120** (Paradigm recurring copy) |\n| A permanent reduces the cost of *other* spells you cast (Affinity granted to your I/S) | Add hook `def static_cost_reduction(self, game, spell, controller) -> int: return 0` to `CardImpl` (`engine/card.py`). In `get_cost_reduction`, after computing `raw = card.cost_reduction(game)`, add `for perm in controller.zones[Zone.BATTLEFIELD].get_all(): raw += getattr(perm, 'static_cost_reduction', lambda *a: 0)(game, card, controller)` **then** clamp to generic as today. Keep the existing clamp/return so `test_cost_reduction.py` stays green (default hook returns 0 → identical behavior). | `engine/casting.py::get_cost_reduction`; `engine/card.py` | **245** (grant affinity to your I/S). Self-affinity for 245 and 1 use the existing `cost_reduction` hook — no new code. |\n| Resolved instant/sorcery goes somewhere other than graveyard (\"exile it instead\") | In `_resolve_spell`, before the non-permanent `move_to_zone(... GRAVEYARD)`, build `ev = MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent(controller=player, owner=card.owner)`, call `ev = game.replacement_manager.apply(game, ev)`, and route to `_DESTINATION_ZONE_MAP[ev.destination]` (import from `engine.zones`) unless `ev.prevented`. Card registers the replacement via `register_replacement_effects`. | `engine/casting.py::_resolve_spell` | **1** (\"if that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it\"). **120** can reuse for Paradigm self-exile (or just `exile()` directly in `on_resolve`). |\n| Flip N coins | Add `def flip_coin(game, player) -> bool: return bool(player.choose_yes_no(\"coin flip: heads?\"))` to `engine/game.py`. Deterministic + scriptable. | `engine/game.py` | **97** (−7 ultimate) |\n| Target player skips their next X turns | Add `self.skipped_turns: dict[int, int] = {}` in `GameState.__init__` (seat → turns owed). In `advance_phase`, in the **else** (no extra_turns) branch, after choosing the normal next index, loop: while that seat has `skipped_turns[seat] > 0`, decrement it, advance `_normal_next_index` past them (i.e. pick `1 - seat`) — i.e. that player's turn is skipped and passes to the opponent. Guard everything behind `if self.skipped_turns:` so the empty-dict path is byte-identical to today (keeps `test_extra_turns.py` green). | `engine/game_state.py::__init__` + `advance_phase` | **97** (−7 ultimate) |\n| Surveil N | Add `def surveil(game, player, n) -> None:` to `engine/game.py`: for each of the top `n` library cards, ask `player.choose_yes_no(\"keep on top?\")` — True leaves it on top, False moves it to graveyard (use `move_zone`/zone `remove`+`add`). Deterministic via script. (Simplest fallback matching `fdn_49`: always to graveyard — but the choose_yes_no version is testable both ways.) | `engine/game.py` | **97** (+1 Surveil 2). Reusable; `fdn_49` inlines its own simplified surveil. |\n| **Converge** (X = colors of mana spent) | **Reuse existing** `card.colors_spent` set by `cast_spell`. `on_resolve` reads `len(getattr(self, 'colors_spent', []))`. | `engine/casting.py` (already) | **4** |\n| **Self** cost reduction ({1} less per X) | **Reuse existing** `cost_reduction(self, game)` override. | `engine/card.py` (already) | **1** (I/S in graveyard), **245** (creatures you control) |\n| Reanimate / put card onto battlefield from graveyard | **Reuse existing** `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)` (fires ETB, registers triggers). | `engine/zones.py` (already) | **97** (−2) |\n| Counter target spell | **Reuse existing** pattern from `cards/fdn/fdn_48` (`_counter_spell`, scan `game.stack.objects()`, `TargetRequirement(zone=Zone.STACK)`). | `cards/fdn/fdn_48` (already) | **57** |\n| Token creation | **Reuse existing** `create_token(game, player, Creature(...))`. | `engine/game.py` (already) | **13** (Inkling), **97**/others if needed |\n\n### Note on \"copy a spell\" (Casualty SOS 226, Prepared SOS 13)\nThere is **no** true spell-copy primitive and \"copies on the stack\" are heavy. Model\ncopies pragmatically as **re-resolving the effect**, not as a second StackObject:\n- SOS 13 Prepared: implement the Swords-to-Plowshares effect inline in the card.\n- SOS 226 Casualty: on the cast trigger, if the player sacrifices a creature, call\n  the just-cast spell's effect a second time (or push a second `cast_spell_free`-style\n  resolution). Keep it engine-limited and documented in a one-line code comment.\nDo **not** add a generic copy engine just for these; it is out of scope.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 2 — Per-card plan\n\nFor each card: oracle clauses → nearest FDN analogue → exact seam(s) → new engine\nwork (cite the gap table) → edge cases worth a test.\n\n### SOS 4 — Together as One  ({6} Sorcery, Converge) — START HERE (simplest)\n- **Clauses**: Converge. Target player draws X; deal X damage to any target; you gain\n  X life. X = number of colors of mana spent to cast it.\n- **Analogue**: `fdn_13` (targets + `on_resolve` reading `chosen_targets`).\n- **Seam**: `get_targets` → two `TargetRequirement`s: (1) a player, (2) \"any target\"\n  (creature or player). In `on_resolve`: `x = len(getattr(self, 'colors_spent', []))`;\n  `draw_card` x times for target player; `deal_damage(game, self, target2, x)`;\n  `controller.life += x`.\n- **New engine**: none (Converge = existing `colors_spent`).\n- **Edge cases**: X=0 when only colorless/generic mana spent (all three do nothing);\n  X=5 with WUBRG; target player = opponent draws; \"any target\" hitting a player vs a\n  creature. In tests, fill the mana pool with the exact colors then cast so\n  `last_payment_colors` is deterministic.\n\n### SOS 226 — Silverquill, the Disputant  ({2}{W}{B} Elder Dragon 4/4)\n- **Clauses**: Flying, vigilance (keywords in spec). \"Each instant/sorcery spell you\n  cast has casualty 1\" — as you cast, you may sac a creature power ≥1; if you do, copy\n  the spell.\n- **Analogue**: `fdn_44` (registers a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` listener — same shape).\n- **Seam**: constructor sets `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.VIGILANCE`,\n  `supertypes={LEGENDARY}`, subtypes `{\"Dragon\",\"Elder\"}`, 4/4. `register_triggers`:\n  register `TriggerRegistration(event_type=SpellCastTriggeredEvent, condition=...,\n  effect=...)` where condition = spell card is I/S AND `event.controller is self.controller`;\n  effect = pick a controlled creature with `power>=1`, if `choose_yes_no` yes →\n  `sacrifice(game, controller, creature)` then re-resolve the spell's effect (copy;\n  see \"copy a spell\" note).\n- **New engine**: gap row 1 (fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` in `cast_spell`).\n- **Edge cases**: no legal sac creature (casualty does nothing); declining the sac;\n  Silverquill's own non-I/S casts don't trigger; the copy targets the same target.\n\n### SOS 257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex  (Land)\n- **Clauses**: `{T}: Add {C}`. `{T}, Pay 1 life: add any color, spend only on I/S`.\n  `{5}: become 2/4 Wizard creature (still a land) with \"whenever you cast an I/S, +1/+0\n  until EOT\"`.\n- **Analogue**: `fdn_245.get_mana_abilities` (tap-for-mana), `fdn_49.get_activated_abilities`\n  (tap ability), `fdn_245.register_triggers` (EOT P/T via ContinuousEffect).\n- **Seam**: subclass `Land`. `get_mana_abilities` → `[ManaAbility(cost=_tap_cost,\n  mana_produced=add {C}), ManaAbility(cost=pay-1-life-and-tap, mana_produced=add chosen\n  color)]`. `get_activated_abilities` → the `{5}` animate ability: pay 5 generic from\n  pool, then mutate self: add `CardType.CREATURE` to `card_types` + `_original_card_types`,\n  set `base_power=2, base_toughness=4, modified_power/_toughness`, `subtypes|={\"Wizard\"}`,\n  init `damage_marked/is_attacking/...` attrs, and register a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`\n  trigger (condition: I/S cast by controller) whose effect adds an EOT `ContinuousEffect(\n  Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS, SubLayer.MODIFY_PT, apply=+1/+0)`.\n- **New engine**: gap row 1 (fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`). The animate is card-local\n  attribute mutation (Land has no `base_power`/combat attrs by default — add them when\n  animating). Restricted \"spend only on I/S\" mana is NOT enforceable — add the mana and\n  leave a one-line `# ENGINE LIMITATION` comment.\n- **Edge cases**: `{T}` ability unavailable while tapped; pay-1-life reduces life;\n  animate only if not already a creature (\"If this land isn't a creature\"); pump stacks\n  per spell cast that turn and resets at cleanup; still a land after animating\n  (`CardType.LAND` retained).\n\n### SOS 245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer  ({6}{B}{G} Elder Dragon 5/5)\n- **Clauses**: Affinity for creatures (self: {1} less per creature you control).\n  Flying, deathtouch. Instant/sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\n- **Analogue**: self-reduction like the `cost_reduction` contract in\n  `engine_tests/test_cost_reduction.py`.\n- **Seam**: constructor `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.DEATHTOUCH`, 5/5, LEGENDARY,\n  `{\"Dragon\",\"Elder\"}`. `def cost_reduction(self, game): return count of creatures\n  self.controller controls` (self-affinity, existing hook). `def static_cost_reduction(\n  self, game, spell, controller): return (creatures controller controls) if spell is\n  I/S and spell.controller is self.controller and self on battlefield else 0` (grants\n  affinity to your I/S).\n- **New engine**: gap row 4 (extend `get_cost_reduction` to sum battlefield\n  `static_cost_reduction`).\n- **Edge cases**: counting Witherbloom itself toward self-affinity (it's not on the\n  battlefield while being cast → not counted, correct); reduction clamped to generic\n  (existing clamp); an I/S you cast while controlling N creatures costs {N} less but\n  never below colored pips; opponent's I/S unaffected.\n\n### SOS 1 — The Dawning Archaic  ({10} Legendary Creature 7/7, Reach)\n- **Clauses**: costs {1} less per I/S in your graveyard; Reach; \"Whenever ~ attacks,\n  you may cast target I/S from your graveyard without paying its mana cost. If that\n  spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\"\n- **Analogue**: `fdn_245` (attack trigger), `fdn_48`/`fdn_13` (targeting), self\n  `cost_reduction` contract.\n- **Seam**: `cost_reduction(self, game)` = count I/S in `self.controller` graveyard.\n  `register_triggers`: `AttacksTriggeredEvent` with condition `event.creature is self`;\n  effect: choose a target I/S in controller's graveyard, `cast_spell_free(game,\n  controller, target, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`, and `register_replacement_effects` /register a\n  `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` replacement on that target redirecting\n  `destination=\"exile\"` (so it exiles when it resolves).\n- **New engine**: gap row 2 (fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent`) + gap row 5 (consult\n  replacements in `_resolve_spell` for stack→graveyard).\n- **Edge cases**: empty graveyard (no target → trigger does nothing / \"may\");\n  cost reduction with 0 I/S in yard = full {10}; reduction never reduces below 0\n  generic (it's all-generic, so it can hit {0}); the free-cast spell ends up in exile,\n  not graveyard, after resolving; Reach present.\n\n### SOS 57 — Mana Sculpt  ({1}{U}{U} Instant)\n- **Clauses**: Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add {C} equal to mana\n  spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\n- **Analogue**: `fdn_48` (counter target spell on the stack).\n- **Seam**: `can_cast`/`get_targets` scan `game.stack.objects()` for a spell (copy\n  fdn_48). `on_resolve`: capture `amount = target.source.mana_cost.cmc` and whether\n  `self.controller` controls a creature with subtype \"Wizard\" **before** countering;\n  `_counter_spell(game, target)`. If a Wizard is controlled, register a one-shot\n  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` trigger (source=self) — condition: it's\n  controller's main phase (`game.active_player is self.controller`) — effect:\n  `self.controller.mana_pool.add(ManaType.COLORLESS, amount)` then unregister itself.\n- **New engine**: gap row 3 (`BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`).\n- **Edge cases**: no Wizard → no deferred mana; \"next main phase\" can be the same\n  turn's postcombat main or next turn's precombat (fire on whichever comes first, then\n  remove the trigger so it doesn't recur); mana empties at phase end so the {C} must be\n  added at the main phase the player will actually use it; nothing on the stack →\n  can't cast.\n\n### SOS 201 — Lorehold, the Historian  ({3}{R}{W} Elder Dragon 5/5)\n- **Clauses**: Flying, haste. Each I/S in your hand has miracle {2}. At the beginning\n  of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card; if you do, draw a card.\n- **Analogue**: `fdn_44` (passive trigger), `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` is already fired\n  by `draw_card`.\n- **Seam**: constructor `Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.HASTE`, 5/5, LEGENDARY. Opponent-upkeep\n  loot: register `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` (already fired) with condition\n  `game.active_player is not self.controller`; effect: `choose_yes_no`; if yes and\n  hand non-empty, `discard` a chosen card then `draw_card`. Miracle: register\n  `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` with condition `event.player is self.controller` AND\n  `event.card` is I/S AND it's the first card drawn this turn\n  (`player.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1`); effect: optionally `cast` the drawn card for an\n  alternative {2} cost — simplest model: temporarily treat its cost as `{2}` and call\n  `cast_spell` (or `cast_spell_free` after manually charging {2} from the pool).\n- **New engine**: none (both events already fired). Miracle is a card-local alternative\n  cost; document the simplification (`# ENGINE LIMITATION: miracle modeled as may-cast\n  for {2} on first draw`).\n- **Edge cases**: only the FIRST card drawn each turn is eligible (use\n  `cards_drawn_this_turn`); only I/S; Lorehold's own upkeep does NOT trigger the loot\n  (only opponents'); declining the discard draws nothing; granting miracle only while\n  Lorehold is on the battlefield.\n\n### SOS 13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares  ({1}{W}{W} Creature 3/3, Prepared)\n- **Clauses**: ETB — target player creates a 1/1 W/B Inkling with flying. Then if an\n  opponent controls more creatures than you, this becomes \"prepared\". While prepared,\n  you may cast a copy of its spell (Swords: exile target creature, its controller gains\n  life = its power); doing so unprepares it.\n- **Analogue**: `fdn_44` token creation + targeting; ETB via `register_triggers` on\n  `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` (condition `event.permanent is self`).\n- **Seam**: constructor `mana_cost=ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{W}{W}\")` (front face), 3/3,\n  LEGENDARY? (spec has no Legendary supertype — it's not legendary; subtypes\n  `{\"Cat\",\"Cleric\"}`), keep a `self._prepared=False` flag. ETB effect: create Inkling\n  token (`create_token(game, target_player, Creature(name=\"Inkling\", base_power=1,\n  base_toughness=1, subtypes={\"Inkling\"}, keywords=Keyword.FLYING))`), then count\n  creatures: if any opponent controls more creatures than controller → `self._prepared=True`.\n  Expose Swords as `get_activated_abilities` returning the prepared ability **only when\n  `self._prepared`** (cost = no-mana / its `{W}` per the back face; pick one and\n  document): effect = exile target creature and `target.controller.life += target.power`,\n  then `self._prepared=False`.\n- **New engine**: none (token + exile + life already exist). \"Cast a copy\" modeled as\n  the inline activated ability (see copy note).\n- **Edge cases**: ETB target player could be the controller or opponent; the \"more\n  creatures\" check counts the just-made Inkling; prepared ability disappears after one\n  use; exiling a creature with 0 power gains 0 life; no creatures to target while\n  prepared.\n\n### SOS 97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer  ({1}{B}{B} Planeswalker, loyalty 3)\n- **Clauses**: +1 Surveil 2. −1 any number of target players each discard a card. −2\n  return target creature MV ≤3 from your graveyard to battlefield. −7 flip 5 coins;\n  target opponent skips their next X turns (X = heads).\n- **Analogue**: `fdn_44` (`Planeswalker`, `get_loyalty_abilities`, `_resolve_target`,\n  `draw_card`/`discard`/`create_token`).\n- **Seam**: subclass `Planeswalker(starting_loyalty=3)`, LEGENDARY, subtypes `{\"Ral\"}`.\n  `get_loyalty_abilities` → four `LoyaltyAbility`:\n  - `+1`: `surveil(game, self.controller, 2)`.\n  - `−1`: each target player `discard` a chosen card (2-player: opponent and/or self).\n  - `−2`: choose target creature card in `self.controller` graveyard with\n    `mana_cost.cmc <= 3`; `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)`.\n  - `−7`: `heads = sum(flip_coin(game, self.controller) for _ in range(5))`; choose a\n    target opponent seat `i`; `game.skipped_turns[i] = game.skipped_turns.get(i,0) + heads`.\n- **New engine**: gap row 6 (`flip_coin`), row 7 (skip-turns in `advance_phase`), row 8\n  (`surveil`). −1/−2 reuse existing helpers.\n- **Edge cases**: surveil with empty/short library; −2 with no ≤3-MV creature in yard;\n  loyalty SBA — Ral dies if loyalty hits 0 (verify SBA handles 0-loyalty PW death; if\n  not, that's a separate engine note, but −7 from loyalty 3 is illegal since cost would\n  drop below 0 — `_activate_loyalty_ability` already rejects it, so −7 needs loyalty ≥7\n  first via +1s); X=0 heads means no turns skipped; skip must not corrupt the\n  `test_extra_turns` FIFO (empty `skipped_turns` ⇒ unchanged path).\n\n### SOS 120 — Improvisation Capstone  ({5}{R}{R} Sorcery — Lesson, Paradigm)\n- **Clauses**: Exile from top of library until total MV ≥ 4; may cast any number of\n  them free. Paradigm: then exile this spell; after first resolving a spell with this\n  name, at the beginning of each of your first main phases you may cast a copy of it\n  from exile free.\n- **Analogue**: `cast_spell_free` (free casts), `fdn_44` (registering a recurring\n  trigger).\n- **Seam**: `on_resolve`: loop `library.top(1)`, exile each (`exile(game, card)`),\n  accumulate `mana_cost.cmc` until `>= 4`; for each exiled card the controller may\n  `cast_spell_free(game, controller, card, Zone.EXILE)`. Paradigm: route this spell's\n  own resolution to exile (use gap row 5 self-replacement, or just `exile(game, self)`\n  at the end of `on_resolve` and skip the default graveyard move by overriding — note\n  `_resolve_spell` will still try to move from STACK; with gap row 5 a self\n  `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent`→exile is cleanest). Register a\n  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` trigger (source = a persistent emblem-like object,\n  since the card itself is in exile): condition = `game.active_player is controller` AND\n  `game.phase is Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN` AND not already done this turn; effect = may cast\n  a fresh copy of Improvisation Capstone from exile free.\n- **New engine**: gap row 3 (`BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`) + gap row 5 (self-exile\n  on resolve; optional — direct `exile` also works).\n- **Edge cases**: library smaller than needed (exile what's there, stop); a single card\n  with MV ≥ 4 stops the loop immediately; declining to cast some/all exiled cards;\n  \"first main phase\" = precombat only (don't fire on postcombat); the recurring trigger\n  must survive the card leaving the stack (own a separate persistent source object so it\n  isn't unregistered).\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 3 — Implementation order\n\nDo the shared engine changes FIRST (each unlocks several cards and is independently\ntestable), then cards simplest→hardest. After each engine change, run `pytest` to\nconfirm `engine_tests/` stays green before building cards on top.\n\n**Phase A — shared engine seams (do these first, in this order):**\n1. **Fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`** in `cast_spell` (gap row 1). One line; no-op\n   until a card listens. Unlocks 226 + 257. *Rationale: smallest, highest-leverage,\n   and `test_cost_reduction.py` integration casts prove it doesn't regress.*\n2. **Fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent`** in `declare_attackers_step` (gap row 2). Unlocks 1.\n   *Rationale: trivial and isolated to combat.*\n3. **Add + fire `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`** in `events.py` + `run_turn`\n   (gap row 3). Unlocks 57 + 120. *Rationale: foundational for two delayed-trigger\n   cards; verify it fires exactly once per main phase.*\n4. **Extend `get_cost_reduction`** with the `static_cost_reduction` hook (gap row 4) +\n   add the default hook to `CardImpl`. Unlocks 245. *Rationale: must keep\n   `test_cost_reduction.py` green — do this deliberately and run that file immediately.*\n5. **Consult replacements in `_resolve_spell`** (gap row 5). Unlocks 1's exile clause\n   (and 120's self-exile). *Rationale: localized to one function; needed before card 1.*\n6. **Add helpers** `flip_coin`, `surveil` to `engine/game.py` + **skip-turns** in\n   `game_state` (gap rows 6–8). Unlocks 97. *Rationale: keep the skip logic behind an\n   `if self.skipped_turns:` guard and run `test_extra_turns.py` right after.*\n\n**Phase B — cards, simplest → hardest (each needs only the seams above + existing infra):**\n7. **SOS 4** Together as One — Converge via existing `colors_spent`. No new engine.\n   *Rationale: pure existing-infra warm-up; validates targeting + resolve patterns.*\n8. **SOS 226** Silverquill — needs seam 1 only. *Rationale: thin card over the cast event.*\n9. **SOS 257** Great Hall — needs seam 1; mana abilities + animate. *Rationale: groups\n   with 226 on the cast-event seam; animate is the only fiddly part.*\n10. **SOS 245** Witherbloom — needs seam 4. *Rationale: groups on the cost-reduction seam;\n    self-affinity reuses the existing hook.*\n11. **SOS 57** Mana Sculpt — needs seam 3; counter pattern from fdn_48. *Rationale: first\n    consumer of the main-phase event; counter logic is well-templated.*\n12. **SOS 201** Lorehold — no new engine (existing draw/upkeep events). *Rationale: two\n    independent triggers; miracle is the only approximation.*\n13. **SOS 13** Emeritus / Prepared — no new engine; ETB + flag + activated ability.\n    *Rationale: Prepared state machine is self-contained but multi-step.*\n14. **SOS 1** The Dawning Archaic — needs seams 2 + 5. *Rationale: combines attack\n    trigger, free-cast, and the exile replacement — build after both seams are proven.*\n15. **SOS 97** Ral Zarek — needs seams 6 (coin), 7 (skip), 8 (surveil). *Rationale:\n    four loyalty modes touching the most new infra; do after the skip mechanism is\n    proven against `test_extra_turns.py`.*\n16. **SOS 120** Improvisation Capstone — needs seams 3 + 5. *Rationale: hardest —\n    exile-until-MV loop, free multi-cast, and a persistent recurring Paradigm trigger;\n    do last, reusing the main-phase event and self-exile already validated by 57 and 1.*\n\n**Cross-cutting test guidance**: for every card write `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`\nusing `test_utils.create_game` / `set_board_state` and `DeterministicPlayer` scripts\n(see `cards/fdn/fdn_13/tests.py`). For mechanics driven by mana colors (4) or coin\nflips (97), script the exact pool/`choose_yes_no` answers so X is deterministic. After\nfinishing all cards, run the full `pytest` to confirm `engine_tests/` and all FDN tests\nremain green.\n","numLines":390,"startLine":1,"totalLines":390}}}
