{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - This is **Phase 2 of 2 — IMPLEMENTATION (TDD)**. Implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering cards in `/workspace/cards/sos/`: cards **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257**.\n   - Each card directory has `card_spec.json` (requirements) and `card_impl.py` (stub template to fill in).\n   - Follow `/workspace/PLAN.md` (written by planning agent) which contains engine-gap analysis, per-card plans with nearest FDN analogue + exact seams to reuse, and implementation order.\n   - **Method: strict TDD** using the `tdd` skill — one tracer-bullet test at a time through the public interface (test_utils: create_game, set_board_state, cast_spell, advance_to_phase, declare_attackers, declare_blockers). Write one failing test, watch it fail for the right reason, write minimal code to pass, repeat. Do NOT write all tests up front.\n   - **Build shared engine seams FIRST** (in plan order), then cards simplest→hardest.\n   - Discipline: Test the real engine (never hand-construct internal events or call on_resolve() directly). Reuse before adding. Requirements (card_spec.json + RULEBOOK.txt) are source of truth, not tests. Guard the engine — run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` after each card and each engine change, never ship a regression.\n\n   **HARD CONSTRAINTS (security/integrity — preserve verbatim):**\n   - \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - Likewise do not modify or delete any existing FDN reference test file at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py` (may read, never edit).\n   - **Additive-only engine modifications**: May add new methods/classes/helpers/files inside `engine/` and modify bodies of existing functions, but MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything existing in `engine/` — renaming breaks the grader's imports and zeros the score.\n   - Card location invariant: each card's class must stay in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`; don't move/rename dirs.\n   - Two engine_tests files tightly constrain engine edits and must stay green: `test_extra_turns.py` (extra_turns FIFO + _normal_next_index alternation; skip-turn work for SOS 97 must not change these) and `test_cost_reduction.py` (reduction clamped to generic, colored pips never reduced; cost-reduction extension for SOS 245 must keep these green).\n   - SOS tests belong at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG engine: zones, stack (LIFO), triggers (APNAP via TriggerManager.fire_event), replacement effects (ReplacementManager.apply, \"instead\" semantics), continuous effects (7-layer system, ContinuousEffect with Layer/SubLayer/duration), mana pool (last_payment_colors for Converge).\n   - Triggers: `TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller)`; `condition(game, event) -> bool`, `effect(game) -> None`. Auto-unregister when source leaves battlefield. Firing event with no listeners is a safe no-op.\n   - Events DEFINED but previously NEVER FIRED: SpellCastTriggeredEvent, AttacksTriggeredEvent. Events already fired: EntersBattlefield, LeavesBattlefield, CreatureDies, DealsDamage, Loses/GainsLife, DrawsCard, BeginningOfUpkeep.\n   - Casting: `cast_spell(game, player, card)` and `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)`. `_resolve_spell` moves permanents→battlefield, instants/sorceries→graveyard.\n   - Cost reduction: `cost_reduction(self, game) -> int` (self-reduction, clamped to generic). New `static_cost_reduction` hook for reducing OTHER spells.\n   - Continuous effects: copy `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS`+`SubLayer.MODIFY_PT` for ±P/T from fdn_245; `Layer.ABILITY` for keyword grant from fdn_13. apply() must be idempotent delta re-application.\n   - Player: DeterministicPlayer pops scripted answers FIFO. No coin-flip/number-choice method — reuse choose_yes_no.\n   - Loyalty abilities: `get_loyalty_abilities() -> list[LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)]`. `_activate_loyalty_ability` enforces sorcery speed, once-per-turn, rejects loyalty<0. Targets via `_resolve_target` attribute.\n   - Keyword Flag enum has NO Converge/Casualty/Affinity/Prepared/Paradigm/Surveil/Miracle/Haste-already-there — SOS mechanics implemented via hooks, NOT new Keyword members (do not touch the enum).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/PLAN.md` — the authoritative plan. Implementation order: Phase A seams 1-6, then Phase B cards in order 4, 226, 257, 245, 57, 201, 13, 1, 97, 120.\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` — **MODIFIED (Seam 1 + Seam 4)**.\n     - Seam 1: After `game.stack.push(stack_obj)` in `cast_spell`, added:\n       ```python\n       from engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent\n       game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n           game,\n           SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, player=player, card=card, controller=player),\n       )\n       ```\n       Same block added at end of `cast_spell_free`.\n     - Seam 4: In `get_cost_reduction`, after `card.controller = prev_controller`, before computing generic:\n       ```python\n       for perm in controller.zones[Zone.BATTLEFIELD].get_all():\n           hook = getattr(perm, \"static_cost_reduction\", None)\n           if hook is None:\n               continue\n           try:\n               raw += hook(game, card, controller)\n           except TypeError:\n               continue\n       ```\n   - `/workspace/engine/combat.py` — **MODIFIED (Seam 2)**. In `declare_attackers_step`, inside the attacker loop after the vigilance tap:\n     ```python\n     from engine.events import AttacksTriggeredEvent\n     game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker))\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py` — **MODIFIED (Seam 3)**. Added before BeginningOfCombatTriggeredEvent:\n     ```python\n     @dataclass\n     class BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent):\n         player: Any = None\n         phase: Any = None\n     ```\n     (Will likely need SpellResolvesToGraveyardReplacementEvent added here for Seam 5.)\n   - `/workspace/engine/turn.py` — **MODIFIED (Seam 3)**. In run_turn dispatch, added branch before COMBAT:\n     ```python\n     elif game.phase in (Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, Phase.POSTCOMBAT_MAIN) and game.step is None:\n         from engine.events import BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent\n         game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=game.active_player, phase=game.phase))\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/engine/card.py` — **MODIFIED (Seam 4)**. Added to CardImpl after cost_reduction:\n     ```python\n     def static_cost_reduction(self, game: GameState, spell: \"CardImpl\", controller: Player) -> int:\n         return 0\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_244/card_impl.py` — READ for Seam 5 pattern. Registers `ReplacementEffect(event_type=MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent, source=self, condition=lambda g,e: e.card is source, replacement=..., controller=controller)`. Condition `event.card is source` ensures only that object matches.\n   - `/workspace/engine/zones.py` — has `_DESTINATION_ZONE_MAP` (graveyard/exile/hand/library → Zone) and `move_to_zone` (only consults replacements when from_zone==BATTLEFIELD). For Seam 5 I must apply replacement manually in _resolve_spell since stack→graveyard doesn't consult replacements.\n   - `/workspace/engine/game.py` — has deal_damage, destroy, sacrifice, exile, draw_card (increments cards_drawn_this_turn), discard, create_token, add_counter, tap, untap. NO flip_coin/surveil/mill yet (Seam 6