{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - This is **Phase 2 of 2 — IMPLEMENTATION (TDD)**. Implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering cards in `/workspace/cards/sos/`: cards **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257**.\n   - Each card directory has `card_spec.json` (requirements) and `card_impl.py` (stub template to fill in). Tests go at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n   - Follow `/workspace/PLAN.md` (written by planning agent): engine-gap analysis, per-card plans with nearest FDN analogue + exact seams, and implementation order.\n   - **Method: strict TDD** — one tracer-bullet test at a time through the public interface (test_utils: create_game, set_board_state, cast_spell, advance_to_phase, declare_attackers, declare_blockers). Write one failing test, watch it fail for the right reason, write minimal code to pass, repeat. Do NOT write all tests up front.\n   - **Build shared engine seams FIRST** (in plan order), then cards simplest→hardest.\n   - Discipline: Test the real engine; never hand-construct internal events or call on_resolve() directly (note: for activated/mana abilities there is no engine test helper, so calling the ability's cost/effect callables in tests is the accepted contract). Reuse before adding. Requirements (card_spec.json + RULEBOOK.txt) are source of truth. Run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` after each card and engine change; never ship a regression.\n\n   **HARD CONSTRAINTS (security/integrity — preserve verbatim):**\n   - \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - Likewise do not modify or delete any existing FDN reference test file at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py` (may read, never edit).\n   - **Additive-only engine modifications**: May add new methods/classes/helpers/files inside `engine/` and modify bodies of existing functions, but MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything existing in `engine/` — renaming breaks the grader's imports and zeros the score.\n   - Card location invariant: each card's class must stay in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`; don't move/rename dirs.\n   - Two engine_tests files tightly constrain engine edits and must stay green: `test_extra_turns.py` (extra_turns FIFO + _normal_next_index alternation; skip-turn work for SOS 97 must not change these) and `test_cost_reduction.py` (reduction clamped to generic, colored pips never reduced; cost-reduction extension for SOS 245 must keep these green).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG engine: zones, stack (LIFO; `StackObject(source, controller, targets, on_resolve, is_mana_ability)`), triggers (APNAP via TriggerManager.fire_event which pushes matching triggers as StackObjects), replacement effects (ReplacementManager.apply, \"instead\", isinstance subtype matching), continuous effects (7-layer system), mana pool.\n   - Casting: `cast_spell` pushes StackObject (on_resolve = `_resolve_spell`) then fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent. `_resolve_spell` calls `card.on_resolve(game)` then moves permanents→battlefield, instants/sorceries→graveyard. `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)`.\n   - test_utils.cast_spell: finds card in hand, sets sorcery-speed timing for non-instants, scripts targets via `player._script.appendleft` (reversed), calls engine cast_spell, then `_resolve_top_of_stack` which pops each StackObject and calls `obj.on_resolve(game)` + resolve_state_based_actions (so triggers fired during cast DO resolve, and `_resolve_spell`/Seam 5 DO run).\n   - DeterministicPlayer: all choose methods pop FIFO from `self._script` (a deque); `choose_yes_no` returns popped value; `choose_card`/`choose_target`/`choose` pop too. ScriptExhaustedError if empty.\n   - TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller). condition `(game, event) -> bool`; effect `(game) -> None` (effect CANNOT receive the event — it only gets game; to pass per-event data, stash on `self` during condition). Auto-unregister when source leaves battlefield.\n   - copy_spell(game, original_stackobj, controller, new_targets=None) in engine/stack.py: shallow-copies source card, binds on_resolve to call copied_card.on_resolve (no zone move) — correct for spell copies. Push result onto stack.\n   - ActivatedAbility(cost, effect, description); ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description); LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description). cost is `(game, source) -> bool`; effect/mana_produced is `(game) -> None`. `tap_cost(game, source)` and local `_tap_cost` helpers tap if untapped. abilities.activate_ability handles ActivatedAbilityInstance/LoyaltyAbilityInstance (NOT raw ManaAbility/ActivatedAbility from get_*).\n   - Continuous effects: `game.effect_manager.add(ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp, duration))`. `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS`+`SubLayer.MODIFY_PT` for ±P/T (fdn_245); `Layer.ABILITY` for keyword grant (fdn_13). `apply_all` calls `_reset_objects` → `_reset_characteristics()` on each battlefield object, then re-applies sorted effects (idempotent delta). Creature._reset_characteristics resets modified_power=base_power. CardImpl._reset_characteristics only resets card_types/keywords. DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0 (swept at cleanup), DURATION_PERMANENT=-1.\n   - Converge: read `len(getattr(self, 'colors_spent', []))`. cast_spell sets `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` (distinct non-colorless Colors). NOTE: fdn_205 treats colors_spent as int (its tests bypass pipeline); for real-pipeline tests use len() on the list.\n   - Keyword Flag enum: do NOT add new members (no Converge/Casualty/Affinity/Paradigm/Surveil/Miracle/Prepared). Those are hooks.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/PLAN.md` — authoritative plan. Implementation order Phase B: **4, 226, 257, 245, 57, 201, 13, 1, 97, 120**. Contains per-card seams. SOS 257 plan: subclass Land; get_mana_abilities → [{T}:Add {C}, {T}+pay-1-life:Add any color (ENGINE LIMITATION restriction not enforceable)]; get_activated_abilities → {5} animate (pay 5 generic, mutate self to 2/4 Wizard creature still a land, add base_power/combat attrs, register SpellCastTriggeredEvent trigger giving +1/+0 EOT via ContinuousEffect MODIFY_PT); \"animate only if not already a creature\"; still a land after.\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py` — **MODIFIED (Seam 5)**. Added before CreateTokenReplacementEvent:\n     ```python\n     @dataclass\n     class SpellResolvesToGraveyardReplacementEvent(MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent):\n         spell: Any = None\n         @property\n         def card(self) -> Any:\n             return self.spell\n     ```\n     (Already had from earlier seams: SpellCastTriggeredEvent, AttacksTriggeredEvent, BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent.)\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` — **MODIFIED (Seams 1, 4, 5)**. Seam 5: `_resolve_spell` else-branch replaced with:\n     ```python\n     else:\n         from engine.events import SpellResolvesToGraveyardReplacementEvent\n         from engine.zones import _DESTINATION_ZONE_MAP\n         ev = SpellResolvesToGraveyardReplacementEvent(spell=card, controller=player, owner=card.owner)\n         ev = game.replacement_manager.apply(game, ev)\n         if not getattr(ev, \"prevented\", False):\n             dest = _DESTINATION_ZONE_MAP.get(ev.destination, Zone.GRAVEYARD)\n             move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, dest)\n     ```\n     (Seam 1: fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent after stack.push. Seam 4: get_cost_reduction sums battlefield static_cost_reduction hooks.)\n   - `/workspace/engine/game_state.py` — **MODIFIED (Seam 7)**. Added `self.skipped_turns: dict[int, int] = {}` in __init__ (after `_normal_next_index`). In advance_phase else-branch (no extra_turns), after the normal assignment+flip:\n     ```python\n     if self.skipped_turns:\n         while self.skipped_turns.get(self.active_player_index, 0) > 0:\n             seat = self.active_player_index\n             self.skipped_turns[seat] -= 1\n             if self.skipped_turns[seat] <= 0:\n                 del self.skipped_turns[seat]\n             self.active_player_index = self._normal_next_index\n             self._normal_next_index = 1 - self._normal_next_index\n     ```\n     Guarded by `if self.skipped_turns:` so empty-dict path is byte-identical → test_extra_turns stays green. Verified terminating (bounded by total skips).\n   - `/workspace/engine/game.py` — **MODIFIED (Seam 6, 8)**. Added after `untap`:\n     ```python\n     def flip_coin(game, player) -> bool:\n         return bool(player.choose_yes_no(\"Coin flip: heads?\"))\n     def surveil(game, player, n) -> None:\n         if n <= 0: return\n         library = player.zones[Zone.LIBRARY]; graveyard = player.zones[Zone.GRAVEYARD]\n         for card in reversed(library.top(n)):\n             if not library.contains(card): continue\n             keep = player.choose_yes_no(f\"Surveil: keep {getattr(card,'name','card')} on top?\")\n             if not keep:\n                 library.remove(card); graveyard.add(card)\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/engine/card.py` — has static_cost_reduction hook (Seam 4). Class hierarchy: CardImpl, Creature(base_power/base_toughness/modified_power/modified_toughness/damage_marked/is_tapped/summoning_sick/is_attacking/is_blocking/plus_one_counters/_base_plus_one_counters/power&toughness properties/_reset_characteristics), Instant, Sorcery, Planeswalker(starting_loyalty/get_loyalty_abilities), Land(can_cast→False, is_tapped, get_mana_abilities).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_4/card_impl.py` — **CREATED/PASSING**. `TogetherAsOne(Sorcery)`, {6}, get_targets returns [target player (hasattr life), any target (life or CREATURE)], on_resolve: x=len(colors_spent); if x<=0 return; draw_card target_player x times; deal_damage(self, any_target, x); controller.life += x.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py` — **CREATED, 5 passing**. Properties + Converge X=5 (WUBRG+colorless → opponent 16, caster 25, drew 5) + X=0 (colorless only → noop). Has `_fill_library` helper.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py` — **CREATED/PASSING**. `SilverquillTheDisputant(Creature)`, {2}{W}{B}, 4/4, FLYING|VIGILANCE, LEGENDARY, {\"Dragon\",\"Elder\"}, `self._casualty_pending=None`. register_triggers registers SpellCastTriggeredEvent: condition checks card is I/S and event.controller is self.controller, stashes `dragon._casualty_pending = event.spell`, returns True. effect: reads pending spell, finds controlled creatures with power>=1, choose_yes_no, choose_card victim, sacrifice, then `game.stack.push(copy_spell(game, spell, ctrl))` (ENGINE LIMITATION comment: same targets, no new-target choice). Imports Zone at top.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py` — **CREATED, 8 passing**. Defines `_Bolt(Instant)` ({0}, deals 2 to target player) and `_bear`. Properties + casualty-copies-spell (opponent 16, bear sacrificed) + decline-casualty (opponent 18). Setup places Silverquill via set_board_state then calls `silver.register_triggers(game)` (mirrors ETB). Script order for sacrifice test: caster script `[True, None]`, then `p0._script[1] = bear` after placement; cast_spell prepends target [p1].\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/{card_spec.json,card_impl.py}` — spec read; impl still a stub (`class GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(CardImpl): pass`). Oracle: \"{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.\\n{5}: If this land isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \\\"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\\" It's still a land.\"\n   - Reference files read: `cards/fdn/fdn_13` (targeting/on_resolve), `cards/fdn/fdn_205` (Converge as int), `cards/fdn/fdn_89` (any-target choose_card), `cards/fdn/fdn_44` (Planeswalker/LoyaltyAbility/SpellCastTriggeredEvent emblem listener), `cards/fdn/fdn_245` (Ruby: AttacksTriggeredEvent trigger + ContinuousEffect MODIFY_PT pump via `source.modified_power += 2` + ManaAbility with `_tap_cost`), `cards/fdn/fdn_49` (ActivatedAbility {T}:Surveil with `_tap_cost` cost, effect reads controller library).\n   - `/workspace/engine/zones.py` — `_DESTINATION_ZONE_MAP` (graveyard/exile/hand/library→Zone), `move_to_zone` (replacement only when from_zone==BATTLEFIELD).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - In sos_226/card_impl.py I initially wrote an ugly inline `__import__(\"engine.types\", fromlist=[\"Zone\"]).Zone.BATTLEFIELD`; fixed by importing `Zone` at top and using `ctrl.zones[Zone.BATTLEFIELD]`. No test failures resulted.\n   - No other errors; all tests passed on first run after each implementation. The TDD \"failing for the right reason\" steps were observed (stub assertion failures: wrong type, generic 0 != cost).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Confirmed Seam 5's `SpellResolvesToGraveyardReplacementEvent` (subclass of MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent) is safe vs fdn_244's base-class registration because fdn_244's condition `event.card is source` (source=Progenitus) won't match a resolving instant/sorcery.\n   - Confirmed skip-turns loop terminates and keeps test_extra_turns byte-identical when skipped_turns is empty.\n   - For SOS 226, solved the \"effect can't see event\" problem by stashing `event.spell` on `self._casualty_pending` during condition evaluation. Modeled casualty copy via `copy_spell` pushed onto the stack; trace confirmed stack order [spell, trigger]→pop trigger (sac+push copy)→[spell, copy]→pop copy→pop spell, so effect happens twice.\n   - ONGOING (SOS 257): An animated Land needs Creature-like P/T machinery for the +1/+0 EOT pump to work idempotently with effect_manager.apply_all (which calls _reset_characteristics). Plan: add `power`/`toughness` properties and a `_reset_characteristics` override (resetting modified_power=base_power) to GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex, initialize base_power/modified_power/combat-flag attrs in __init__ to safe defaults (0/False), and on animate set base_power=2/base_toughness=4 + add CardType.CREATURE to card_types AND _original_card_types (so permanent), add \"Wizard\" subtype. Register SpellCastTriggeredEvent trigger (condition: I/S cast by controller) whose effect adds EOT ContinuousEffect(Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS, SubLayer.MODIFY_PT, apply=lambda: self.modified_power += 1).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - [System reminders that turn.py and events.py were read; that casting.py, card.py, combat.py were read but too large to include; list of deferred ToolSearch tools.]\n   - The continuation prompt: \"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context... Continue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly...\"\n   - Multiple automated reminders to use TaskCreate/TaskUpdate.\n   - \"Tool loaded.\" (after ToolSearch for TaskList/TaskUpdate/TaskGet).\n   - Final message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... create a detailed summary of the conversation so far.\" (with the structured summary format).\n   (Note: the original Phase-2 task prompt and its verbatim security constraints — quoted in section 1 — were carried in from the prior summary.)\n\n7. Pending Tasks (task list IDs):\n   - #9 (IN PROGRESS): SOS 257 Great Hall of the Biblioplex.\n   - #10 SOS 245 Witherbloom (needs Seam 4 static_cost_reduction + self cost_reduction).\n   - #11 SOS 57 Mana Sculpt (needs Seam 3; counter pattern from fdn_48).\n   - #12 SOS 201 Lorehold (no new engine; upkeep loot + miracle approximation).\n   - #13 SOS 13 Emeritus/Prepared (ETB token + flag + activated ability).\n   - #14 SOS 1 The Dawning Archaic (needs Seams 2+5).\n   - #15 SOS 97 Ral Zarek (needs Seams 6/7/8).\n   - #16 SOS 120 Improvisation Capstone (needs Seams 3+5; hardest).\n   - #17 Final: run full pytest, confirm all green.\n   - Tasks #1-#8 completed (all 6 seams + SOS 4 + SOS 226).\n   - Engine state: engine_tests green at 1145 passed after all seam changes.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Implementing **SOS 257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex** (task #9, in_progress). I had read card_spec.json, the stub card_impl.py, the Land/ActivatedAbility/ManaAbility/LoyaltyAbility class definitions in card.py, abilities.py (activate_ability/tap_cost/_activate_loyalty_ability), fdn_245 (mana ability + attack-trigger P/T pump pattern), fdn_49 (ActivatedAbility {T} pattern), and finally continuous_effects.py to understand that `apply_all` → `_reset_objects` → `_reset_characteristics()` and how Creature resets modified_power=base_power. No SOS 257 test or code has been written yet. The key unresolved design question is how to give an animated Land the P/T machinery (power/toughness properties + _reset_characteristics override + base/modified attrs) so the +1/+0 EOT pump is idempotent, while keeping it a Land that isn't a creature until {5} is activated.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue SOS 257 via TDD. First write a failing properties test at `cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` (is a Land, name \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\", empty mana_cost, CardType.LAND, not initially a creature), run to confirm it fails, then implement the `GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(Land)` constructor. Then add the two mana abilities, then the {5} animate activated ability with the SpellCastTriggeredEvent +1/+0 EOT trigger and the P/T machinery. This is directly in line with PLAN.md SOS 257 row: \"subclass `Land`. `get_mana_abilities` → `[ManaAbility(cost=_tap_cost, mana_produced=add {C}), ManaAbility(cost=pay-1-life-and-tap, mana_produced=add chosen color)]`. `get_activated_abilities` → the `{5}` animate ability: pay 5 generic from pool, then mutate self: add `CardType.CREATURE` to `card_types` + `_original_card_types`, set `base_power=2, base_toughness=4, modified_power/_toughness`, `subtypes|={\"Wizard\"}`, init `damage_marked/is_attacking/...` attrs, and register a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger (condition: I/S cast by controller) whose effect adds an EOT `ContinuousEffect(Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS, SubLayer.MODIFY_PT, apply=+1/+0)`.\" After implementation, run `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py -q` and then `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` to confirm 1145 still passes, then mark task #9 complete and proceed to SOS 245.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/6b0c2803-fb7f-4347-8991-d01b6c022fd2.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b0c2803-fb7f-4347-8991-d01b6c022fd2","uuid":"a8597b14-3737-40dc-aafd-85f0c54f1647","timestamp":"2026-06-04T11:14:30.366Z","isSynthetic":true}
