{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **Phase 2 of 2 — IMPLEMENTATION (TDD)**. Implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering cards in `/workspace/cards/sos/`: cards **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257**.\n   - Each card directory has `card_spec.json` (requirements) and `card_impl.py` (stub template to fill in). Tests go at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n   - Follow `/workspace/PLAN.md` (planning agent's plan): per-card plans with nearest FDN analogue + exact seams, and implementation order.\n   - **Method: strict TDD** — one tracer-bullet test at a time through the public interface (test_utils: create_game, set_board_state, cast_spell, advance_to_phase, declare_attackers, declare_blockers). Write one failing test, watch it fail for the right reason, write minimal code to pass, repeat. Do NOT write all tests up front.\n   - **Build shared engine seams FIRST** (done — all 8 seams complete), then cards simplest→hardest.\n   - Discipline: Test the real engine; never hand-construct internal events or call on_resolve() directly (for activated/mana abilities there is no engine test helper, so calling the ability's cost/effect callables in tests is the accepted contract; firing documented TriggeredEvents through trigger_manager.fire_event to simulate the triggering moment is used for trigger tests). Reuse before adding. Requirements (card_spec.json + RULEBOOK.txt) are source of truth. Run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` after each card and engine change; never ship a regression.\n\n   **HARD CONSTRAINTS (security/integrity — preserve verbatim):**\n   - \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - Likewise do not modify or delete any existing FDN reference test file at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py` (may read, never edit).\n   - **Additive-only engine modifications**: May add new methods/classes/helpers/files inside `engine/` and modify bodies of existing functions, but MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything existing in `engine/` — renaming breaks the grader's imports and zeros the score.\n   - Card location invariant: each card's class must stay in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`; don't move/rename dirs.\n   - Two engine_tests files tightly constrain engine edits and must stay green: `test_extra_turns.py` and `test_cost_reduction.py`.\n   - Do NOT modify `test_utils.py` (test helper at workspace root; grader may use its own copy — treat as off-limits, work around its constraints instead).\n   - Keyword Flag enum: do NOT add new members (no Converge/Casualty/Affinity/Paradigm/Surveil/Miracle/Prepared). Those are hooks/flags on the card.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG engine: zones (Zones object, accessed via `player.zones[Zone.X]` — NOT `.get()`), stack (LIFO; StackObject(source, controller, targets, on_resolve, is_mana_ability)), triggers (TriggerManager.fire_event pushes matching triggers as StackObjects in APNAP order), replacement effects, continuous effects (7-layer system), mana pool.\n   - TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller). condition `(game, event) -> bool`; effect `(game) -> None` (effect CANNOT receive the event — stash per-event data on `self` during condition). Auto-unregister when source leaves battlefield. `trigger_manager.unregister(source)` removes all triggers with that source (use for one-shots; instants never on battlefield so won't auto-unregister).\n   - fire_event pushes trigger StackObject with `on_resolve=trigger.effect`. Resolve via `_resolve_top_of_stack(game)` (pops, calls obj.on_resolve(game), runs SBA).\n   - test_utils.cast_spell: requires EMPTY stack (raises \"stack is not empty\" at line 277 unconditionally). Scripts targets via `player._script.appendleft` (reversed). Calls engine cast_spell then `_resolve_top_of_stack` (resolves whole stack). For counterspells (need spell on stack), bypass via `from engine.casting import cast_spell as engine_cast_spell` + manual `_resolve_top_of_stack`.\n   - DeterministicPlayer: choose/choose_card/choose_target/choose_yes_no/assign_damage_order all pop FIFO (popleft) from `self._script` deque. ScriptExhaustedError if empty. `create_game(scripts=([...p0...],[...p1...]))`.\n   - Casting (engine/casting.py): get_cost_reduction sums `card.cost_reduction(game)` + each battlefield permanent's `static_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)`, clamped to generic. cast_spell enforces mana payment (can fail with CastingError). `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)`. cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone) casts without paying (used for miracle). Targets stored on StackObject → set as `card.chosen_targets` at resolve.\n   - Continuous effects: `game.effect_manager.add(ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp=0, duration))`. `apply_all(game)` → `_reset_objects` (calls `_reset_characteristics()` on each battlefield object) then reapplies sorted effects (idempotent). NOT called by test harness — call explicitly to observe. `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS`=7, `SubLayer.MODIFY_PT`=\"7c\". DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0, DURATION_PERMANENT=-1. Creature.power = modified_power + plus_one - minus_one.\n   - ManaPool: `.add(mt, n)`, `.pay(ManaCost)`, `.can_pay(cost)`, `.get(mt)`, `.total()`, `.empty()`. ManaCost.parse(\"{5}\"), ManaCost has `.cmc`, `.generic`, `.pips`.\n   - Engine fires EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent BEFORE register_triggers (zones.py L307-315) so self-ETB triggers won't fire on natural entry — tests must register_triggers then manually fire EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent(permanent=card). Established FDN pattern (fdn_98): condition `event.permanent is source`.\n   - Events: EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent(permanent, controller, card, creature); DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card) — fired by draw_card which increments `player.cards_drawn_this_turn`; BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent() (NO fields — use `game.active_player is not self.controller` to detect opponent's upkeep); BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, phase); SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller); AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker).\n   - game.py helpers: exile(game, obj), create_token(game, player, token) (sets is_token/owner/controller, fires ETB, calls register_triggers), draw_card, discard, deal_damage, sacrifice, destroy. flip_coin(game, player), surveil(game, player, n) added in Seam 6-8.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py` — **CREATED/PASSING (10 tests)**. `GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(Land)`. Module-level `_ANY_COLOR_MANA = (WHITE,BLUE,BLACK,RED,GREEN)` and `_tap_cost(game, source)`. __init__ inits dormant creature attrs (base_power=0, modified_power=0, plus/minus counters, damage_marked, summoning_sick, is_attacking, is_blocking, is_token, _is_animated=False, _animate_trigger_registered=False). `_reset_characteristics` override (super + reset modified_power=base_power etc). `power`/`toughness` properties. `get_mana_abilities` returns [{T}:Add{C}, {T}+pay-1-life:Add chosen color via `ctrl.choose(list(_ANY_COLOR_MANA),...)`]. `get_activated_abilities` returns {5} ability (cost pays ManaCost.parse(\"{5}\"), effect calls `_animate`). `_animate`: guard `if self._is_animated or CardType.CREATURE in self.card_types: return`; sets base_power=2/base_toughness=4, adds CREATURE to card_types AND `_original_card_types = frozenset(self._original_card_types | {CardType.CREATURE})`, adds \"Wizard\" subtype, calls `_register_animate_trigger`. Trigger: SpellCastTriggeredEvent, condition (is creature + I/S cast by controller), effect adds EOT ContinuousEffect(Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS, SubLayer.MODIFY_PT, apply=lambda: source.modified_power += 1).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` — **CREATED, 10 passing**. `_NoOpInstant({0})`. Properties + mana abilities (colorless, any-color pays 1 life) + animate (becomes 2/4 Wizard still LAND, mana spent) + pump on instant cast (call ability.cost/effect, cast_spell \"Ping\", `game.effect_manager.apply_all(game)`, assert power==3, idempotent) + animate-only-if-not-creature (double activate → still +1 only).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py` — **CREATED/PASSING (10 tests)**. `WitherbloomTheBalancer(Creature)`, {6}{B}{G}, 5/5, FLYING|DEATHTOUCH, LEGENDARY, {\"Dragon\",\"Elder\"}. Module `_count_creatures(player)` uses `player.zones[Zone.BATTLEFIELD]`. `cost_reduction(game)` = `_count_creatures(self.controller)`. `static_cost_reduction(game, spell, controller)`: return 0 if controller is not self.controller or spell not I/S, else `_count_creatures(controller)`.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py` — **CREATED, 10 passing**. `_bear`, `_Spark(Instant, configurable cost)`. Properties + self-affinity (3 bears → {6}{B}{G} cast with {3}{B}{G}, pool empty) + no-creatures-no-reduction + grants-affinity-to-instant (Witherbloom+2 bears → {3} Spark cast with {1} leftover) + opponent-instant-unaffected.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py` — **CREATED/PASSING (7 tests)**. `ManaSculpt(Instant)`, {1}{U}{U}. Module `_get_chosen_target(card)`, `_counter_spell(game, stack_obj)` (removes from `game.stack._items`, moves card from controller STACK zone to owner graveyard). `_spell_targets(game)` scans `game.stack.objects()`. `can_cast`/`get_targets` (TargetRequirement zone=STACK). `on_resolve`: capture `amount = target.source.mana_cost.cmc`, `controls_wizard = self._controls_wizard()`, `_counter_spell`, then if wizard and amount>0 `_register_deferred_mana(game, amount)`. `_controls_wizard` scans battlefield for \"Wizard\" subtype. `_register_deferred_mana`: BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent trigger, condition `game.active_player is source.controller`, effect adds COLORLESS amount then `game.trigger_manager.unregister(source)` (one-shot).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py` — **CREATED, 7 passing**. `_NoOp(Instant, configurable cost)`, `_wizard`, `_push_victim(game, idx, cost)` (uses engine_cast_spell, returns (card, stack_obj)), `_sculpt_mana()`={COLORLESS:1,BLUE:2}, `_cast_with_target(game, player, card, target)` (player._script.appendleft(target); engine_cast_spell; _resolve_top_of_stack). Properties + counter + deferred-mana-with-wizard (fire BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=p0,phase=PRECOMBAT_MAIN), _resolve_top_of_stack, assert COLORLESS==4; one-shot check) + no-wizard-no-mana.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py` — **CREATED/PASSING (13 tests)**. `LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature)`, {3}{R}{W}, 5/5, FLYING|HASTE, LEGENDARY, {\"Dragon\",\"Elder\"}, `self._miracle_card=None`. Module `_is_instant_or_sorcery(card)`. register_triggers registers two: (1) loot BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent, condition `game.active_player is not source.controller`, effect choose_yes_no then choose_card discard + draw_card; (2) miracle DrawsCardTriggeredEvent, condition (card not None, event.player is controller, is I/S, `event.player.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1`) stashes `source._miracle_card=card`, effect choose_yes_no then if can_pay({2}) pay + cast_spell_free(game, ctrl, card, Zone.HAND). Has `# ENGINE LIMITATION: miracle modelled as a may-cast for {2}` comment.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` — **CREATED, 13 passing**. `_LifeGain(Instant, {5}, gains 3 life)`, `_filler`. Properties + loot (opponent upkeep, set active_player_index=1, script [True, discard_me]) + loot-declined + no-loot-own-upkeep + miracle-first-draw (set cards_drawn_this_turn=0, draw_card, _resolve_top_of_stack, life==23, mana==0) + declined + only-first-card (card